target/
node_modules/
www/pkg/
# The root .gitignore's `.gm/*` rule is anchored to the repo root (a gitignore
# pattern containing a slash is relative to the file that declares it), so it
# does NOT cover nested tool state elsewhere in the tree. One `.gm/` landed
# under www/ after a tool ran with that cwd and got committed; the browser verb
# also creates `.agentplug/` there. These basename-only rules match at every
# depth in this crate, so serving a different subdirectory cannot recur under a
# new path.
.gm/
.agentplug/
